5 years\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Voyager 2's encounter with Jupiter was optimized in part to ensure that future planetary flybys would be possible\",\n      \"line\": 3,\n      \"span\": \"Its encounter with Jupiter was optimized in part to ensure that future planetary flybys would be possible\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The Uranus encounter's geometry was defined by the possibility of a future encounter with Saturn\",\n      \"line\": 3,\n      \"span\": \"The Uranus encounter's geometry was also defined by the possibility of a future encounter with Saturn\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Voyager 1 had only 6.4 days of close study during its flyby\",\n      \"line\": 3,\n      \"span\": \"Voyager 1 had only 6.4 days of close study during its flyby\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Voyager 2 became the first human-made object to fly past Uranus\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"Voyager 2 became the first human-made object to fly past Uranus\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Voyager 2's observations began on January 24, 1986\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"Its observations began on January 24, 1986\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Signals took approximately 2,5 hours to reach Earth\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"signals took approximately 2,5 hours to reach Earth\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Light conditions were five-hundred times less than terrestrial conditions\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"Light conditions were five-hundred times less than terrestrial conditions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Closest approach to Uranus took place at 17:59 on January 24, 1986\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"Closest approach to Uranus took place at 17:59 on January 24, 1986\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Closest approach was at a range of about 50,640 kilometers (81,500 miles)\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"at a range of about 50,640 kilometers (81,500 miles)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Voyager 2 discovered 11 new moons\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"discovered 11 new moons\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The moons were given names Pucka, Portila, Juliette, Kressida, Rosalinde, Belinda, Desdemona, Cordelina, Ophelia, and Bianca II\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"given such names as Pucka, Portila, Juliette, Kressida, Rosalinde, Belinda, Desdemona, Cordelina, Ophelia, and Bianca II\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A naming tradition was begun in 1687\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"continuing a naming tradition begun in 1687\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Voyager 2 discovered three new rings\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"three new rings\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"There were eight \\\"older\\\" rings\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"the \\\"older\\\" eight rings\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A magnetic field was tilted at 66 degrees off-axis and off-center\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"a magnetic field tilted at 66 degrees off-axis and off-center\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Wind speeds in Uranus' atmosphere reached as high as 450 km/h (72400 meters per hour)\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"wind speeds in Uranus' atmosphere as high as 450 km/h (72400 meters per hour)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Evidence was found of a boiling lake of water some 479 miles (900 kilometers) below the top cloud surface\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"found evidence of a boiling lake of water some 479 miles (900 kilometers) below the top cloud surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Uranus's rings are extremely variable in thickness and transparency\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"Its rings were found to be extremely variable in thickness and transparency\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Voyager 2 returned photos of Miranda, Oberon, Ariele, Umbrella, and Titan\",\n      \"line\": 9,\n      \"span\": \"returned spectacular photos of Miranda, Oberon, Ariele, Umbrella, and Titan\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Miranda, Oberon, Ariele, Umbrella, and Titan are five of Uranus' smaller moons\",\n      \"line\": 9,\n      \"span\": \"five of Uranus' smaller moons\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Voyager 2 flew by Miranda at a range of only 17.560 miles (28.260 kilometers)\",\n      \"line\": 9,\n      \"span\": \"flying by Miranda at a range of only 17.560 miles (28.260 kilometers)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The spacecraft came closest to any object so far in its nearly century-long travels during the flyby of Miranda\",\n      \"line\": 9,\n      \"span\": \"came closest to any object so far in its nearly century-long travels\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Uranus itself appeared generally featureless\",\n      \"line\": 9,\n      \"span\": \"Uranus itself appeared generally featureless\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The news of the Uranus encounter was interrupted the same day by the Challenger accident\",\n      \"line\": 11,\n      \"span\": \"was interrupted the same day by the tragic Challenger accident\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The Challenger accident killed six astronauts\",\n      \"line\": 11,\n      \"span\": \"that killed six astronauts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The Challenger accident occurred during a space shuttle launch\",\n      \"line\": 11,\n      \"span\": \"during their space shuttle launch\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The Challenger accident occurred on January 28, 1986\",\n      \"line\": 11,\n      \"span\": \"on January 28, 1986\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":144120,"type":"result","duration_ms":152622,"uuid":"8bfd7e97-5608-4cbe-97cb-e86556630cb8","ttft_stream_ms":1024,"time_to_request_ms":91,"first_content_frame_ms":1025,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
